From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:49:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] nodes shader: per-vertex fog in the vertex color's
 alpha

The node fragment shader received eyeVec (a vec3) only to compute the fog
clarity, and spent a length() per pixel on it. With dynamic shadows off
nothing else reads it. The vertex shader now computes the clarity, in
full precision, and passes it in varColor.a, which was always 1.0 and
unused; the fragment shader reads it. On Mali-400 (Mesa lima) that is one
varying less per vertex for the GPU to write and read back, and the fog
no longer depends on fp16 precision in the fragment stage.

Map faces are one node wide, so interpolating the clarity per vertex
looks the same as computing it per pixel.

Upstream: not sent yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/client/shaders/nodes_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl b/client/shaders/nodes_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl
index e0d88afb4..f462448e0 100644
--- a/client/shaders/nodes_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl
+++ b/client/shaders/nodes_shader/opengl_fragment.glsl
@@ -596,8 +596,7 @@ void main(void)
 	// As additions usually come for free following a multiplication, the new formula
 	// should be more efficient as well.
 	// Note: clarity = (1 - fogginess)
-	float clarity = clamp(fogShadingParameter
-		- fogShadingParameter * length(eyeVec / fogDistance), 0.0, 1.0);
+	float clarity = varColor.a;
 	float fogColorMax = max(max(fogColor.r, fogColor.g), fogColor.b);
 	// Prevent zero division.
 	if (fogColorMax < 0.0000001) fogColorMax = 1.0;
diff --git a/client/shaders/nodes_shader/opengl_vertex.glsl b/client/shaders/nodes_shader/opengl_vertex.glsl
index b65671609..ea26b06ac 100644
--- a/client/shaders/nodes_shader/opengl_vertex.glsl
+++ b/client/shaders/nodes_shader/opengl_vertex.glsl
@@ -5,6 +5,8 @@ uniform vec3 dayLight;
 // The cameraOffset is the current center of the visible world.
 uniform highp vec3 cameraOffset;
 uniform float animationTimer;
+uniform float fogDistance;
+uniform float fogShadingParameter;
 
 VARYING_ vec3 vNormal;
 // World position in the visible world (i.e. relative to the cameraOffset.)
@@ -214,7 +216,8 @@ void main(void)
 	nightRatio = 1.0 - color.a;
 	color.rgb = color.rgb * (color.a * dayLight.rgb +
 		nightRatio * artificialLight.rgb) * 2.0;
-	color.a = 1.0;
+	// fog clarity rides in the alpha: fp32 here, the fragment stage may be fp16
+	color.a = fogShadingParameter - fogShadingParameter * length(eyeVec) / fogDistance;
 
 	// Emphase blue a bit in darker places
 	// See C++ implementation in mapblock_mesh.cpp final_color_blend()
